// bff-edge is the public gRPC gateway that multi-region calabi-edges use
// to reach the control plane. Edges in the same Kubernetes cluster as
// the control plane can still dial each microservice's ClusterIP
// directly — bff-edge only matters for cross-region edges (cn-hangzhou
// ECS → cn-chengdu ACK control plane), where the control-plane svcs
// stay private and bff-edge fronts them on a single mTLS gRPC port.
//
// The wire shape mirrors what calabi-edge already calls on identity-svc /
// tunnel-svc / cert-svc / quota-svc / config-svc + a handful of
// NATS-subject pumps wrapped as server-streams (cert events, session
// evict, usage deny/allow). Reverse direction (edge → NATS publish of
// usage reports) is collapsed into a regular unary RPC.
//
// Authn: mTLS client cert, CN = "edge-{edge_node_id}-{region}". bff-edge
// parses the CN, looks the edge up in identity-svc, and injects the
// resolved edge_node_id into the request context. Every RPC handler
// overwrites the edge_node_id field on incoming requests with the
